```
void test (int a, int *c, int *d) {
  if (a)
   *c = a;
  else
   *d = a;
}
```

## What?
This PR implements three changes:

### 1. displayManifestErrorLoading
It adds color `red` to `displayManifestErrorLoading` function to better highlight these kinds of messages.

### 2. Validation
This PR is adding a more detailed validation to the manifest options which is expected to be of the following type.:

```
{
  "options": {
    "name": string;
    "value":string;
  }[]
}
```
The following checks are now applied and shows to the user. This validation does not break the process and instead just shows a message to the user to adapt changes.  Here is a list of new checks and messages.

> [!WARNING]  
> This incorrect validation seems to be happening in two places: `@storyblok/manifest-helper` and `field-plugin/helpers/vite`.

1. Empty object `{}` :  Incorrect object value. Must be of type {"name": string, "value": string}.
2. Incorrect type `{"name": "test", "value": 0}`: Incorrect value type. Must be of type string.


![CleanShot 2024-09-17 at 08 39 01](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/58b91703-e677-495f-9040-9f37d2793027)


### 3. @storyblok/manifest-helper 
Turns `@storyblok/manifest-helper` has been turned into internal package and is consumed by `packages/field-plugin/helpers/vite` helper instead of having duplicated code. 

